      "referendumTitle": "Renewal of Wayne County Zoological Authority Millage in Support of the Detroit Zoo",
      "referendumText": "In 2008 and 2016,\u00a0pursuant to\u00a0Public Act 49 of 2008,\u00a0Wayne\u00a0County voters renewed a 10-year\u00a0property tax millage to fund zoological services through the\u00a0Wayne\u00a0County Zoological\u00a0Authority, supporting animal care for more than 2,000 animals and 200 species,\u00a0educational\u00a0and senior programs, and facility maintenance at the Detroit Zoo.\u00a0To continue providing these services, the Authority seeks to renew and restore the millage to\u00a0the original voter-approved rate of 0.10 mill (10 cents per $1,000 of taxable value). This\u00a0proposal would renew the millage at 0.0982\u00a0mill and restore the remaining 0.0018\u00a0mill that was\u00a0reduced due to required rollback, for a total authorized rate of 0.10 mill on taxable real and\u00a0personal property\u00a0for ten (10) years.\u00a0If approved, the millage rate would be unchanged from those approved by voters in 2008 and\u00a02016. Funds will be disbursed to the Authority and transferred to the Detroit Zoo as\u00a0permitted\u00a0by law. All funds are subject to annual independent audits. It is estimated that $6,145,462 will\u00a0be collected in the first year.\u00a0Ballot Question:\u00a0Do you approve the renewal and restoration of the levy of 0.10 mill on all taxable property in\u00a0Wayne\u00a0County for a period of ten (10) years, from 2028 through 2037?\u00a0",
